MajorDuties:
This is a Direct Hire Public Notice, under this recruitment, applications will be accepted for each location and/or installation identified in this Public Notice and selections are made for vacancies as they occur. There may or may not be actual/projected vacancies at the time you submit your application. This position is being filled under Direct Hire Authority (DHA) in accordance with Section 1109 of FY 2020 NDAA; P.L. 116-92 and Section 9905 of Title 5, U.S.C. This Public Notice is to gather applications which may or may not result in a referral or selection.This Public Notice is to gather applications which may or may not result in a referral or selection.Please read this Public Notice in its entirety prior to submitting your application for consideration. As a INTERDISCIPLINARY, GS-0801/1301/1515-15, your typical work assignments may include the following:Serves as an expert advisor for naval aviation, including carrier air wing (CVW), tactical air (TACAIR) platforms, tactics and procedures, sensors, weaponry, Naval Integrated Fire Control (NIFC), advanced electronic warfare (EW)/attack/electronic protection systems, and command, control, communications, computers, intelligence, surveillance and reconnaissance (C4ISR). Perform studies and analyses under the supervision of the Deputy Director for Air Warfare Systems, OSD(DOT&amp;E). He or she reviews operational test documents to support operational effectiveness, suitability, and survivability evaluations for major defense acquisition programs. Responsible for computer modeling and simulation techniques employed in the area of OT&amp;E including those used in associated highly classified programs, combined developmental (DT) and operational test (OT) and architectural studies. Incumbent will address and resolve issues for highly classified programs when given responsibility for and access to those programs. Provide expert assistance, advice, and support to the DOT&amp;E and is responsible for oversight, monitoring, and test observance of Air Warfare Systems programs, such as: CVN-78, MQ-25, Next Generation Jammer (NGJ), NIFC, and advanced electronic warfare and threat systems. The incumbent must ensure adequate OT&amp;E is planned and executed on the Major Defense Acquisition Program (MDAP) military system in accordance with Title 10, United States Code, and associated DoD Directives. The incumbent's responsibilities also include the following functions:
a. Provision of guidance on the conduct and evaluation of operational testing to OSD, the military Departments, and theDefense Agency elements;
b. Development of systems and stands for the administration and management of operational testing policies and procedures;
c. Prescription of operational testing policies and procedures;
d. Issuances of DoD directives and other publication pertaining to OT&amp;E;
e. Monitoring and review of all operational testing activities;
f. Review of Test and Evaluation Master Plans, Mission Element Need Statements, System Concept Papers, Development Concept Papers and Integrated Program Summaries for OT&amp;E implication;
g. Coordination of OTs conducted jointly by two or more services;
h. Initiate, conduct, and review of plans, programs actions, and tasking to ensure adequate design of OT&amp;E;
i. Approval of adequacy of OT plans;
j. Analysis, evaluation, and assessment of the results of OT;
k. Submission of operational test reports to the Secretary of Defense and to Congress.
l. Preparation of the DOT&amp;E Annual Report on OT&amp;E activities of the DoD and to the Congress.
m. Review of OT&amp;E studies submitted by Military Departments and Defense Agencies.
n. Preparation of response to request and correspondence from Congress, the Government Accounting Office, and theInspector General on operational test matters.
o. Development and administration of an OT&amp;E database;
p. Participation in activities of the Defense Acquisition Board and the Defense Planning and Resources Boards; and
q. The incumbent, as an analyst, shall:
(1) Formulate strategic Air Warfare Systems level OT&amp;E plans and provide modeling assistance to Operational TestAgencies (OTAs) level planning groups and evaluation teams;
(2) Maintain close liaison with Services, their research and development agencies and OTAs on their OT&amp;E model andsimulation efforts;
(3) Participate in Air Warfare Systems, CVW TACAIR and NIFC systems, weaponry and C4ISR systems test andevaluation (T&amp;E) test plan working groups for the integration of system and mission C4ISR systems into plans,assessments, and reports.

